<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Sep industrial output falls 6.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore Sep industrial output falls 6.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output in September fell by 6.8 percent compared to the same month of the previous year after falling 7.2 per cent in August, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement cumulative growth for manufacturing in the first nine months of 1996 was 4.8 percent.</p>
<p>Table of Singapore's top 10 industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				     Sep 96	 Aug 96	 July 96</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	-6.8	   -7.2	    1.7</p>
<p>    Electronics		  -7.4	   -4.7	    8.7</p>
<p>    Fabricated Metals	  -8.2	   -7.4	   -3.8</p>
<p>    Transport Equipment     -18.9	  -18.4	   -5.0</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics  -8.3	   -7.7	    5.2</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	 14.9	   -4.3	   -6.8</p>
<p>    Paints, pharmaceuticals -11.4	  -25.7	  -15.9</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	-6.1	   -3.2	   -4.0</p>
<p>    Industrial chems/gas	nil	   -0.3	    nil</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	-0.4	   -0.6	   -2.8</p>
<p>Plastic products -13.9 -15.2 -5.8</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
